context_title:
BUMP—I arrive in a custom pink hearse, pearl rims, velvet trim; let it glide;
CLICK—my Sri Lankan homegirl, bangles jangling, gloss poppin’, rides at my side;
POP—Schiaparelli, Jelly Belly; Polly Pocket purse with the front-row glow;
SWISH—Willy Wonka and Slugworth on payroll; my ruffles make sugar-clouds snow.
TAP—Bottega bows, satin rose; little handbag with empires inside;
SNAP—Dior on the door, couture to the floor; all the avenues curtsy worldwide;
ᵗᵉᵉ⁻ʰᵉᵉ—lip gloss, big boss; I’ve got lace-gloved battalions in tow;
He holds the title “king,” but I’m the woman conquering the territory, row by row.
—CUT—glittering tenant, I’m bitter, demented; I seize our shared skull—hostile acquisition;
I eat competitors’ brains by the spoonful; their clever endeavors fuel my superior flow—cerebral nutrition;
Goblins, ghouls, wraiths—my relatives; shredding your sentences syllable-first is a bloodline tradition;
Who handed this industry’s keys to these counterfeit caretakers—who signed for this demolition?
Erratic emphatics, acrobatic attacks; I stampede through the snare, eradicate inhibition;
Riddle the meter, get quicker, get meaner; no inhale, no foothold, no intermission;
Incinerate imitation, accelerate agitation; your catalog’s ash in my composition;
She claws at our palate; I swallow her protest, bolt up our jaw—unconditional submission.
Veterans. Ten-hut. Set your dusty awards down. I need respect.
“Rookie”? Look alive. Your résumé can’t negotiate my check.
Your feature: $5,000. Mine pays TEN TIMES that. Count the stacks.
ONE feature verse: $50,000—even though I haven’t released my debut studio album. Facts.
Signed. Not estimated. Cleared. Not promised. Trace the transaction.
Say, “You’re paid more.” No hedging. No excuses. No redaction.
My cash stacks block the skylight. Harness. Handholds. Boots. Start climbing.
Bow at the summit. Tell your peers who sets the price of rhyming.
BUMP—lip-gloss, grip-lock; I headlock competitors, kidnap the critics, silk-ribbon restraints and the custom pink hearse disappearing into night;
Eyes HERE! Eyes HERE! LOOK HERE! LOOK HERE! Crowd and contenders, surrender your retinas, no eyelid vacations—I own every sliver of sight;
CLICK—silk skip, bass rip; one tongue, two tyrants; she bounces in satin, I pounce through the patterns; together we drag every snare off the track;
From Dubai to Versailles—imperial glitter, arterial jitters—I make both hemispheres buckle and kneel when this hijacked ribcage talks back;
Eyes on ME! Eyes on ME! LOOK AT ME! LOOK AT ME! You with the headphones, you gripping a mic—no peripheral privileges; don’t you dare disappear;
Kneel to the heel and the growl in the gloss; relinquish ambition, submit without conditions, lay names at our feet—only “yes” is permitted in here;
Pink nails on the fader; she’s delicate, decadent, smiling inside me; my thunder starts stuttering, sugar-sweet treason is reaching to repossess me;
BOOM—chestquake, breath-break, syllable avalanche, larynx in overdrive; surrender your focus, your throne, your tomorrow—DON’T TOUCH THE FADER—I AM A MONSTER! ᵗᵉᵉ⁻ʰᵉᵉ

